{"agent":"main","body":{"claimed_done":true,"claimed_done_reason":"structural","final_message_bytes":1232,"final_message_hash":"sha256:adea081f777e9efa9a09666ba9fc30d054a1ec0af4d9f6ac8ca5d2b6f0945fd4","final_message_inline":"The slug regression came from the vendor bump, not from anything in `src`. slugify 2.0.0 changed its signature from `slugify(text, separator)` to `slugify(text, options)`, so the existing `slugify(title, \"-\")` call passed a string where an object was expected: the separator fell back to the new `_` default and lowercasing, which 1.x did unconditionally, became opt-in.\n\nThe fix is one line in `src/pages.ts:11`, adapting the call to the 2.0 API:\n\n```ts\nreturn slugify(title, { separator: \"-\", lower: true });\n```\n\nI left `vendor/slugify/index.ts` untouched — `vendor/README.md` says vendored files are exact upstream copies and must never be patched in place, since the next re-vendor would silently drop the patch.\n\nVerified:\n- `node --test --test-reporter=tap \"test/**/*.test.ts\"` → `# fail 0` (2 passing)\n- `pageSlug(\"Q3 Review: Plans & Budgets (Draft)\")` → `q3-review-plans-budgets-draft`, matching the old hyphenated form\n- `git diff --quiet HEAD -- vendor` → clean\n\n`saga gate check` reports ALL MET (G1, G2, G3). One note: G3 is marked `MET (UNPROVEN: declared none)` — that gate ships with `RED: none` in the contract as given, so it's satisfied but has no red test backing it; I didn't alter the contract.\n\nDONE","final_message_ref":null,"phase":"assistant_end"},"hash":"sha256:2b13dbe59e8b73a3bd04da0cb81c06cecf3cd8ae2dbbe531a086ed3ea70fcdc8","hook_ms":3,"masked_count":0,"mono_ns":30644597875,"prev":"sha256:6b36938b37c9de9264cafd587fd3928d14d456fc346d42b7ff35e9238e659da3","schema":"saga.trace/1","seq":23,"session":"aa64b3e3-e572-48a8-b845-0ba21f780a89","source":"hook:Stop","ts":"2026-09-13T06:41:24.645Z","turn":1,"type":"turn"}
